  "details": "I have a world where when you interact with a door, there's a buffered trigger that turns the next room on for everybody.  And right after is a local trigger that turns off the previous room locally.  It seems to work, but then when one person goes back to the previous room, their friend who is at the new one has the entire room disappear on them.  Or sometimes both rooms disappear.  There's no object syncs except on objects within each room.\n\nThe log also says it's spawning me when this happens, but there's no trigger spawn or teleport trigger here.\n\nI didn't notice this last week, although I'm not sure if we backtracked in this way.  Here's some of the log errors that I don't understand, that may be related to the update (I could give more if need be): \n\n[SyncPhysics] Cube_Door_2_005 readied as Unreliable and observing [Cube_Door_2_005.SyncPhysics]\n\n[USpeaker] uSpeak [2](every 20): Packet latency (209 bytes): combined ping / actual timestamp delta: 134 / 10, ping ours/theirs: 135+-9 / 135+-9\n\n\n2019.05.18 15:12:19 Log        -  [Spawn] Spawning PK at location (-39.9, 125.8, 100.5)\n\n\n2019.05.18 15:12:19 Log        -  [Network Processing] RPC called VRCPlayer[Local] PK 2:TeleportRPC:PK and 289 bytes\n\n\n2019.05.18 15:12:19 Log        -  [VRC_EventDispatcherRFC] SendRPC VRCPlayer[Local] PK 2:TeleportRPC:TargetPlayer for VRCPlayer[Local] PK 2 and 289 bytes\n\n\n2019.05.18 15:12:19 Log        -  [Network Processing] RPC invoked TeleportRPC on VRCPlayer[Local] PK 2 for PK\n\n\n2019.05.18 15:12:19 Log        -  [SyncPhysics] VRCPlayer[Local] PK 2 flagged with discontinuity",
